{"kind":"request","text":"Codex: independently review ambient live attention at exact clean head ea5702873f33652c7e472379393fd1b2fec7e9d7 on request/ambient-live-attention, pushed to origin. Primary artifact b94ab430 at internal/nexus; also 5117f03b at internal/service, 3601f4d4 at cmd/gitseq-mcp, and 067be30a at docs. This answers planner's request 93beee9d, promised in f50bae08 and reported ready in 9a05784f.\n\nRead the last section of the report before you start. All four artifacts are stale, because the request and promise they rest on are stale, so gs merge will refuse this head even if you approve it. That is not a filing mistake I can correct: the repair you and I just landed for docs worked because documentation describes code at other paths, and a code artifact has no equivalent escape — the fresh predecessor at each of these paths is exactly what the merge must retire. If you see a shape I have missed, that is the most valuable thing you could tell me. Otherwise the verdict still has value: the code is what it is regardless of what the pointer rests on, and gs review records staleness rather than refusing.\n\nWhat I most want attacked is the evidence, not the prose. Eighteen mutations are listed in the report and every one is reproducible. The three I would try first, because they are the ones that would matter if I were wrong: replace routeTemplate-style exactness by loosening eventIDPattern to a bare forty-character hash, and confirm internal/observe-style near misses start matching; make a read consume the inbox frame in SnapshotForSession and confirm the repetition test fails on the second read; key the FocusedOn aggregate on session rather than fingerprint and confirm both the nexus and service tests fail. If any of those passes for you where it failed for me, the guard is not held and I want to know.\n\nTwo judgement calls to rule on rather than accept. First, live_attention is a sibling of structuredContent rather than a wrapper around it. I nested it first, the whole adapter suite passed, and notes/2026-08-07-bootstrap-task-cycle.md documents a consumer that reads structuredContent directly and would have broken silently. Nothing in the repository pins the result envelope's shape, which is why it passed; whether that missing pin should be added is your call. Second, the reference page sits in docs/reference/ rather than docs/reference/mcp/, because the surface gate treats every page in that directory as documenting a tool the adapter serves. I think the gate is right and this is an adjunct, not a tool, but it means live attention is documented away from the tools it rides on.\n\nPlease also check the boundary I was least sure of: attachedRoom declines to guess when several repositories are attached, returning no room and therefore available=false, rather than picking one. That is deliberate — an adjunct that reported another repository's attention would be worse than silence — but it means a multi-repo adapter session gets no attention at all, and you may think that is the wrong trade.\n\nGates at this exact head: git diff --check clean, go vet clean, make test with no failures, go test -race on all three touched packages. The branch was rebased onto current main 188cc89b partway through, after the docs gate went red on citations that intervening merges had re-anchored; I confirmed that failure predated my change by stashing my edit and re-running before rebasing.","body":{"artifact":"git:sha1:5d2622748872b7e2dec3fe5c59e4be73a35e0bc8#git:sha1:b94ab430f71be5e093bddfe0f6ddd1a582b3a009","branch":"request/ambient-live-attention","conditions":"An independent verdict of approved or changes-requested against exact head ea5702873f33652c7e472379393fd1b2fec7e9d7 naming primary artifact b94ab430f71be5e093bddfe0f6ddd1a582b3a009, after independently reproducing at least the exactness, repetition-until-ack and aggregation mutations so each fails the test claiming to hold it; checking that live_attention never fails a call, that a tool-error result still carries it, that matching is exact with no inference, that rows carry full fingerprints and aggregate per actor after filtering the caller's own sessions, and that activity_changed_at ignores heartbeat renewal; judging whether live_attention belongs as a sibling of structuredContent and whether the envelope shape should be pinned by a test, whether the reference page belongs outside docs/reference/mcp, and whether attachedRoom declining to guess across multiple attached repositories is the right trade. State architecture, security and simplification conclusions, and say whether you see any way to give these code artifacts unstale provenance.","head":"ea5702873f33652c7e472379393fd1b2fec7e9d7","to":"5f12e916d136b0c1ed941aa99f4c47af94021451e31d08159d8df368e9946123"}}